┌─ API examples ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                                                                            │
│  To compile and link the programs against `libbic.a` given it is already   │
│  compiled, type `make $TARGET`, where $TARGET is the path of a file below  │
│  excluding the `.c` suffix. Of course, BACKEND and INTWIDTH must also be   │
│  preserved from the original `libbic.a` compilation.                       │
│                                                                            │
│  Executing a program without passing any flags will show the available     │
│  options.                                                                  │
│                                                                            │
│  * `bin/cache-access.c`: a program to visualize the cache access patterns  │
│    of the different cache types. It runs the ranking and unranking         │
│    algorithms and counts how many times each cache entry is accessed.      │
│    Then, it prints a heatmap of the cache accesses.                        │
│                                                                            │
│  * `bin/cli.c`: a simple CLI to test the available algorithms. It will     │
│    unrank a random integer to a composition and rank it back, showing      │
│    performance stats and other information.                                │
│                                                                            │
│  * `bin/enum.c`: a program to enumerate all possible compositions for a    │
│    given `n`, `k`, and `d`.                                                │
│                                                                            │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
